-----Original Message-----
From: Márcio Laurini <mpla...@gmail.com>
To: r-inla-disc...@googlegroups.com
Subject: [r-inla] problem with libpardiso.so in inla binary install
Date: Fri, 18 Mar 2022 21:36:58 -0300

Dear INLA users
We are having an issue which seems to be caused by the incompatibility
of the standard INLA package with Redhat based systems. The cluster we
are running INLA on is based on the Centos 7 distribution. We first got
the following message:
"/lib64/libm.so.6: version `GLIBC_x.xx' not found"
To try to fix it, we tried the binary version of INLA. Thereafter, the
following message appeared:
 "/scratch/apps/gnu/R-
4.1.1/lib64/R/library/INLA/bin/linux/64bit/inla.mkl: error while loading
shared libraries: libpardiso.so: cannot open shared object file: No such
file or directory".
We were not going to use pardiso in this application due to new
licensing issues, but it seems that even in this situation the package
depends on this library.

Márcio Laurini

